{
  "slug": "housekeeping",
  "name": "Housekeeping",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Keep your Claude Code configuration under version control with zero friction. The /houseKeeping command detects changes to your ~/.claude directory – settings, memory files, skills, hooks – stages everything, commits with a descriptive message, and pushes to your remote. Never lose a config tweak again.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `houseKeeping` (Commit and push any changes to the global Claude Code configuration repo at ~/.claude).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install housekeeping@claude-community` from `yoelf22/claude-housekeeping-plugin`.\n\nThis project has moved to claude-code-housekeeping — a simpler, single-file slash command that does the same thing without the plugin overhead.",
